ITEMS=[]
def family(options,rows):
 assert len(options)==len(rows)==4
 for i,(q,e) in enumerate(rows):ITEMS.append((q,[options[i]]+options[:i]+options[i+1:],e))
family(['Self-defence under section13','Occasional activities under section15','Dedicated activities under section16','Private collection under section17'],[
('An individual demonstrates a need for a lawful ordinary handgun for personal protection that cannot reasonably be met by other means. Which licensing purpose addresses that need?','Section13 concerns an eligible firearm for self-defence, subject to its requirements; a need is not an automatic entitlement.'),
('An applicant participates in recreational hunting from time to time and applies on the occasional basis rather than dedicated status. Which licensing category is relevant?','Section15 addresses occasional hunting and sports-shooting.'),
('An active sports participant applies with the required declaration from the accredited organisation supporting dedicated status. Which licensing category is relevant?','Section16 concerns dedicated hunting and dedicated sports-shooting, supported by the required association declaration.'),
('An accredited collectors association approves a firearm for its historical interest, and the applicant seeks to hold it as a private collector. Which category is relevant?','Section17 concerns firearms in a private collection and requires the applicable association support.')])
family(['A licence-renewal application','A change-of-address notification','A change-of-circumstances notification','An application for a duplicate document'],[
('An owner wants a current licence to continue beyond its approaching expiry date. Which process addresses that objective?','Renewal under section24 addresses the continued validity of an expiring licence.'),
('A licence holder moves house while the firearm and licensing purpose remain unchanged. Which notification specifically addresses the new residential location?','Section25 requires written notification of changed physical or postal address.'),
('Material information supplied in an application changes, but neither the physical nor postal address changes. Which general notification is relevant?','Section26 requires notification of changes to information submitted with the application.'),
('A current licence card is damaged so that its details are no longer legible. The licence itself has not expired. Which application addresses the damaged document?','Section29 provides for a copy when a document is defaced, lost or stolen; this is distinct from renewing the licence.')])
family(['Within24hours','Within7days','Within30days','At least90days before expiry'],[
('A holder discovers that a firearm licence card has been stolen. How soon must the loss or theft be reported to the Registrar under section29?','The report is due within24hours of discovering the loss or theft. Applying for a copy is a separate duty.'),
('A licence card has been defaced. Within what period after discovering this must the holder apply for a copy under section29?','An application for a copy must be made within7days of discovery of defacement, loss or theft.'),
('A licence holder changes a postal address. Within what period must written notification reach the Registrar under section25?','The holder must notify the Registrar in writing within30days after the address change.'),
('An owner wishes to renew an ordinary firearm licence. What is the statutory advance filing requirement under section24?','The renewal application must be made at least90days before the licence expires.')])
family(['1licence','2licences','3licences','4licences'],[
('Ignoring any other licensing category, what is the maximum number of section13self-defence licences one person may hold?','Section13 permits no more than one licence under that section.'),
('A person has one section13licence and one section15licence, with no additional licences. How many more section15licences could fit the numerical ceiling, assuming all other requirements are met?','A section13holder may hold three section15licences. With one already held, two numerical places remain.'),
('A person holds one section13licence and no additional licences. What is the total numerical ceiling for that person\'s section15licences?','Section15(3)(b) reduces the section15ceiling to three when the person holds a section13licence.'),
('A person holds no section13licence and no additional licences. What is the ordinary total numerical ceiling for section15licences?','Section15 ordinarily permits up to four licences, subject to its handgun and other restrictions.')])
family(['Continued residence on the same premises','Compliance with the licence requirements','A separate licence for each firearm','An express business purpose on the licence'],[
('An applicant seeks a section12additional licence for a firearm already licensed to another resident. Which residential connection is required?','Section12 additional licences are linked to living on the same premises as the holder of the primary licence.'),
('A spouse assumes that a section12additional licence is automatic because the primary holder already qualified. What must the spouse independently satisfy?','Every additional licence holder must comply with all requirements for the issue of the relevant licence.'),
('An applicant buys two ordinary firearms and assumes one firearm licence can cover both without separate licensing. What principle in section11corrects this?','Each firearm requires a separate licence, even if a single document happens to contain more than one licence.'),
('A company obtains a firearm licence under section20. What must the licence specify to delimit the permitted business use?','A section20 licence must specify the business purpose for which it is issued, and use is limited accordingly.')])
family(['Seek the Registrar\'s endorsed permission to use','Obtain written consent for disposal','Comply with the stated authorisation conditions','Apply for the appropriate ordinary licence'],[
('A section21temporary authorisation allows possession but contains no endorsement permitting use. Before any lawful use under that authorisation, what additional permission is needed?','Section21(5) requires the Registrar\'s endorsement permitting use and compliance with the relevant conditions.'),
('A person wants to dispose of a firearm held under a section21temporary authorisation. Which approval specifically addresses disposal?','Section21(6) requires the Registrar\'s written consent for disposal, subject to any imposed conditions.'),
('A temporary authorisation specifies where the firearm may be kept. What obligation applies throughout the temporary period?','Temporary authorisation is conditional; noncompliance can lead to withdrawal.'),
('An heir wants to keep an inherited ordinary firearm permanently, rather than merely hold it temporarily for disposal. What licensing step is required?','Section148 requires the appropriate licence, permit or authorisation. Inheritance alone does not confer possession rights.')])
family(['The firearm\'s identifying mark','The applicant\'s personal identity','The authority to possess that firearm','The authorised storage location'],[
('A police record must distinguish one firearm from another identical model. Which information directly identifies the individual firearm?','The manufacturer\'s serial number or another authorised identifying mark distinguishes the firearm.'),
('A DFO checks that the person submitting an application is the person named in the supporting identity document. Which matter is being verified?','Identity verification concerns the applicant, rather than the firearm\'s serial number.'),
('A buyer presents a shop receipt but is asked for the licence, permit or authorisation covering the firearm. What legal matter is the official checking?','A receipt shows a transaction; lawful possession requires the applicable authority under the Act.'),
('A written temporary-storage permission specifies a particular street address. Which part of the arrangement does that address define?','The firearm must be stored in the prescribed safe at the place specified in the storage authorisation.')])
family(['2years','5years','10years','The period fixed by the Registrar'],[
('Under section27, what is the ordinary validity period of a section14restricted-firearm self-defence licence?','The statutory table gives a section14licence a two-year period, subject to termination and renewal provisions.'),
('Under section27, what is the ordinary validity period of a section13self-defence licence?','The statutory table provides five years for section13, subject to termination or renewal.'),
('Under section27, what is the ordinary validity period of a section15occasional hunting or sports-shooting licence?','The statutory period is ten years for section15, subject to the Act\'s termination and renewal rules.'),
('What sets the duration of a section21temporary possession authorisation, rather than an ordinary licence?','The Registrar determines the period of temporary authorisation; no universal ordinary-licence term applies.')])
family(['An accredited hunting association','An accredited sports-shooting organisation','An accredited collectors association','The licensed security service provider'],[
('A dedicated-hunting application needs the statutory declaration supporting the applicant\'s registered membership. Which organisation supplies it through its chairperson or written delegate?','Section16 requires the declaration from the relevant accredited hunting association for a dedicated hunter.'),
('A dedicated sports participant needs the section16membership declaration. Which organisation provides it through the authorised representative?','The relevant accredited sports-shooting organisation supplies the declaration for dedicated sports status.'),
('A private collector needs the statutory declaration supporting collector status and approved collection interest. Which organisation is relevant?','The accredited collectors association provides the support required by section17.'),
('A security officer is issued a company firearm for authorised work. Which entity must hold the business firearm licence and ensure the officer has the required competency?','Section20 requires the security service provider holding the business licence to supply only to a competent security officer in its service, subject to the prescribed conditions.')])
family(['Obtain lawful authority before possession','Use the formal correction procedure','Notify the Registrar about illegible markings','Return the lapsed additional licence'],[
('A relative offers an ordinary firearm as a gift. The recipient has no licence, permit, authorisation or other applicable permission for it. What must precede permanent possession?','A gift does not override the general possession prohibition; obtain the appropriate legal authority before possession.'),
('A newly issued licence contains a clerical mistake. What should the holder do instead of changing the printed details personally?','Regulation108 provides a prescribed correction application through the DFO. Personal unauthorised alteration is prohibited.'),
('An owner discovers that the firearm\'s identifying mark has become illegible, without having altered it. What notification is required?','Section23(6) requires notification to the Registrar forthwith when the identifying mark has become illegible or has been tampered with.'),
('A section12holder has moved away from the primary licence holder\'s premises and the additional licence has lapsed. What must be done with that document?','Section12 requires the lapsed additional licence to be returned to the Registrar forthwith.')])
family(['7days','30days','60days','6months'],[
('A company nominates a new competent responsible person under section7. Within what period from nomination must it notify the Registrar?','Section7(4) requires written notification within seven days of nomination.'),
('Before cancelling a licence under section28(2), how much written notice must the Registrar give for the holder to submit representations?','Section28(3) provides thirty days\' written notice for representations before cancellation.'),
('After receiving a section28cancellation notice, what is the ordinary period for disposing of the firearm through a dealer or as the Registrar determines, absent an extension?','Section28(4) provides sixty days after receipt of the notice, with a possible extension on good cause.'),
('An association\'s accreditation under the relevant section8provision is cancelled and notice is gazetted. Within what period must registered members join another relevant accredited association?','Section8(4)(a) gives members six months from publication of the notice to join another relevant accredited body.')])
family(['Trustworthiness and integrity','Suitability for the relevant function','Capacity to serve the accredited purpose','Capacity to advance the Act\'s purposes'],[
('An accreditation review investigates whether an organisation\'s officers provide honest records and act reliably. Which statutory criterion most directly concerns that evidence?','Section8 includes trustworthiness and integrity among the minimum accreditation criteria.'),
('An accreditation review asks whether an organisation is appropriate to perform the particular statutory role it seeks. Which criterion is directly being assessed?','Suitability to perform the relevant functions is distinct from merely having sufficient resources.'),
('An organisation seeks recognition for a role but lacks the personnel and systems needed to carry it out. Which accreditation criterion most directly concerns this shortfall?','Capacity to serve the purpose of the accreditation concerns whether the organisation can perform the proposed role.'),
('A proposed accredited organisation can operate its own activities but has no ability to support the broader statutory objectives of lawful control. Which criterion is specifically in question?','Section8 also requires capacity to advance the purposes of the Act, beyond the organisation\'s own operations.')])
family(['A sale','A donation','A loan','A letting arrangement'],[
('Ownership is transferred in exchange for an agreed purchase price. Which transaction is described, and remains subject to the Act\'s transfer controls?','Selling is included in the statutory definition of transfer; payment does not dispense with lawful-possession requirements.'),
('A person gives a firearm to another without receiving payment and intends the recipient to keep it. Which type of transfer is described?','A donation is a transfer under the Act and still requires lawful authority for possession.'),
('An owner hands over a firearm for a temporary period without a hire charge, with return expected. Which type of transfer is described?','Lending is included in transfer. Ownership remaining with the lender does not remove the Act\'s requirements.'),
('A person supplies possession for an agreed period in return for a rental charge. Which type of transfer is described?','Letting is included in transfer; a hire arrangement cannot substitute for the legally required authority.')])
family(['Express authority to possess firearms','The intended purpose of possession','The limit on how long possession endures','The nominated responsible individual'],[
('A trust deed describes its charitable goals but says nothing permitting possession of firearms or ammunition. Which section7trust-deed element is missing?','The deed must clearly provide for possession of the relevant firearms, ammunition or muzzle loading firearms.'),
('A trust deed permits firearm possession but does not say why the trust would possess them. Which required deed element is missing?','The deed must clearly stipulate the intended purpose of possession.'),
('A trust deed permits possession for a stated purpose but omits the condition that possession lasts only while needed for that purpose. Which required element is missing?','Section7 requires possession to endure only while necessary to achieve the stated intended purpose.'),
('A company has completed its internal approval but has not identified any natural person to make its firearm application on its behalf. What appointment is still required?','A juristic applicant must nominate a natural person to act as its responsible person under section7.')])
family(['Identify the challenged decision','State the date of the decision','Set out the grounds of appeal','Attach supporting written submissions'],[
('An appeal notice says the applicant disagrees with the Registrar but does not identify what was refused or cancelled. Which required element is missing?','Regulation91 requires the notice to identify the decision being appealed.'),
('An appeal notice identifies the refusal and explains the objection, but omits when the Registrar made the decision. Which required element is missing?','The date of the decision must be stated and is relevant to the appeal period.'),
('An appeal notice identifies a decision and its date but gives no reasons why it should be changed. Which required element is missing?','The notice must clearly state the ground or grounds of appeal.'),
('An appellant has drafted separate written arguments supporting the appeal but has not included them with the notice. What required step remains?','Regulation91 requires supporting written submissions to accompany the appeal notice.')])
assert len(ITEMS)==60
